      <h2>Nursery and Kindergarten</h2>
      <p><strong>Nursery</strong> has two teachers in the room all day. Mornings are short bursts of learning: a story, a song, a puzzle. Then lunch, a nap and a gentle afternoon.</p>
      <p><strong>Kindergarten</strong> starts every day outside, then phonics and maths, then literacy. After the nap comes Understanding the World: science and geography for four-year-olds.</p>
      <p>Both groups pick up English from the room. Most of our youngest children arrive with none.</p>
