<section class="faq">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Questions parents ask</h2>
    <details><summary>Does my child need any English to start?</summary><p>No. Most of our youngest children arrive with none. They pick it up from the room.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can we start with a few days a week?</summary><p>At first, yes: most children start with short days, as above. Once settled it is a full-time program, and tuition is the same however many days your child comes. We take children from 20 months.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What about nappies and naps?</summary><p>Nappies are fine. Please send spare nappies and wipes, a change of clothes and a plastic bag. There is a two-hour nap every day, and each child has their own cot.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What time is pick-up?</summary><p>15:15. After-care until 16:30 is available for an extra fee. Drop-off is from 8:00 to 8:30.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is there a progress report?</summary><p>Yes. Early Years families get a written progress report describing what their child is exploring and what comes next.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

